{"full":"hf:wrrwrr111/LuminaStudio","spaceId":"wrrwrr111/LuminaStudio","name":"Lumina Studio","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":9,"created":"2026-01-19T02:47:51.000Z","updated":"2026-01-21T11:02:25.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://wrrwrr111-luminastudio.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/wrrwrr111/LuminaStudio","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T21:22:22.635Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T21:22:22.635Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T21:22:22.635Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"✨","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An experimental FDM engine exploring layered optical color mixing. Starting with CMYK pixel art, evolving into a universal multi-material photo processor.","Lumina-Layers bridges the gap between digital pixels and physical filaments.","Traditional multi-color relief tools rely on theoretical \"Transmission Distance\" (TD) values, which often fail due to filament batch variance, nozzle temperature, or slicer logic. Lumina-Layers uses a Closed-Loop Calibration System. By scanning a physically printed color matrix, it builds a \"Ground Truth\" Look-Up Table (LUT) specific to your printer hardware, ensuring accurate color reproduction for pixel art and relief models."],"features":["Perfectly consistent filament dye concentration","Identical nozzle temperatures across all materials","Uniform layer adhesion","Different filament brands/batches","Printer models and nozzle designs"],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/wrrwrr111/LuminaStudio/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0ef6e1511cb1dc44c6a89c090d860c400afedb4966c37e3299a6b55db93b0823","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T21:22:22.781Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T21:22:22.781Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An experim